# W31 (2026-08-28): the .png sources Joe drops next to each rendered photo.
# Nothing imports them, so they never reach a build — they are 2 MB each of
# repository weight for no shipped byte.
# ⚠️ Ignoring them makes a png-without-webp SILENT, which is the failure mode
# this repo has spent a day removing. scripts/check-dist.mjs warns by name when
# a photo has a .png and no matching .webp.
# ⚠️ That warning can only fire where the .png exists — locally. CI never sees
# an ignored file, so this is a local safety net, not a CI one.
# ⛔ Deliberately narrow: photos only, not a blanket *.png.
src/assets/photos/*.png

# W37 follow-up (2026-08-28): the same thing happens in design/, where Joe drops
# the 2880x1200 masters (4-6 MB .png beside a ~100 KB .webp). Only the .webp is
# ever copied into src/assets/ and shipped.
# ⛔ NOT a blanket ignore of design/: that directory also holds the logo and
# favicon set, which are archival and must stay tracked.
# ⚠️ 10 of the .png files already in this directory ARE tracked (the logo and
# favicon renders). A gitignore rule does not untrack anything, so they are
# unaffected — but that also means this pattern would silently stop tracking
# them if one were ever `git rm --cached`ed. Verified after adding: all 13
# design/ entries still listed by `git ls-files design/`.
design/*.png
